{#
compose/_discard.stream.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The draft is gone: drop every row that stood for it and empty the window's
frame. For an in-place draft the frame lives inside the row, so the remove
already takes it with it.

Both removes address ids that only exist in the view the draft was opened
from — the conversation row when reading a thread, the list row in Drafts —
and a turbo-stream remove aimed at an absent id is a no-op, so each view gets
exactly the one that applies to it.

Variables: messageId, frame, inline, threadId (null unless the thread is now
empty)
#}
<turbo-stream action="remove" target="thread_message_{{ messageId }}">
</turbo-stream>

{% if threadId is not null %}
    <turbo-stream action="remove" target="thread_{{ threadId }}">
    </turbo-stream>
{% endif %}

<turbo-stream action="update" target="{{ frame }}">
    <template></template>
</turbo-stream>
